\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar{\loch
A few years ago I submitted an entry which used a Raspberry Pi Pico\u8217\'92s PIO subsystem as a 0-30MHz quadrature signal generator. That idea has been taken to a considerably higher level by Jon Dawson and his design published online in GitHub and 101 Things. I am sure that he did not copy my signal generator design because it seems to be an obvious thing to do with it.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The SEMARC club has chosen this project for 2026 and will design PCBs and housings.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar{\loch
His PicoRX is a fully-featured minimal-cost long-wave to 30MHz receiver and decodes AM, FM, LSB, USB and CW. All it requires is a \u163\'a35 Pico, cheap OLED display, 3 push-buttons, shaft encoder, cheap dual op-amp and a multiplexer IC, plus a few resistors and capacitors. The receiver can be improved by the addition of band-pass filters and an Si5351 module if one really wants to splash out. His design uses surface-mount low-pass filters but my build will use larger components with legs, for experimentation.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The Pico has two 12-bit ADCs and they collect I and Q samples from a low IF of DC to 12kHz. Oversampling is enabled and that gives an improvement on the dynamic range. A pre-amp would be useful for the higher bands but on 40m the performance is perfectly acceptable thought broadcast interference could be an issue at night. There is excellent AGC, all done in software.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Another brilliant feature is the USB interface which provides audio output and CAT commands. This is similar to rigs costing \u163\'a31,000. FLDIGI can be used to decode RTTY, PSK and MFSK signals. I have also used it with EI5DI\u8217\'92s SD logger. It also runs under DXLab Commander, so a PC can be used to select mode and frequency. CAT control is sent to COM3 on this Windows PC.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Because the minimum build would cost about \u163\'a310 + PCB, it is ideal for schools. There are 512 memories covering not only Amateur bands but also LW, MW and SW broadcast stations, plus all the 27MHz CB channels. These may be easily changed and downloaded into the Pico.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\hich\af3\dbch\af8\langfe2052\dbch\af6\afs24\alang1081\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f3\fs24\lang2057\kerning1\ql\ltrpar\loch

